  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are two identical sound sources of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>656</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. The source&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is located at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> moves anti-clockwise with a uniform speed&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;on a circular path around <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>, as shown in the figure. There are three points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> on this path such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> are diametrically opposite while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is equidistant from them. A sound&nbsp;detector is placed at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. The source <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> can move along direction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></math>.</p>\n\n<p>[Given: The speed of sound in air is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>324</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/2ccb586b-f0a0-4329-b62a-091f10e6cc9f.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 226px;\" /></p>\n<br>Consider both sources emitting sound. When&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;approaches the detector with a speed&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>,&nbsp;the beat frequency measured by the detector is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hz</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8.2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/1729a4c3-65cb-44fe-aa8f-31f796efe0a3.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 223px;\" /></p><p>Given:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>656</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>324</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Frequency heard due to movement of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>324</mn><mrow><mn>324</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>656</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>324</mn><mn>320</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>656</mn></math></p><p>And frequency heard due to movement of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;would be same as that of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>, because the direction of velocity at position&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is perpendicular to the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></math>, so there is no relative change in position at that moment.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>656</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Beat frequency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>656</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>324</mn><mn>320</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
